{"pattern_name": "Command Injection via Runtime.exec()", "functionality": "The code executes a system command based on the operating system, reads the command's output, and returns it as a string. It handles both successful and failed command executions.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The vulnerability arises when user-controlled input is directly passed to the `Runtime.exec()` method without proper sanitization or validation. This allows an attacker to inject arbitrary commands by manipulating the input string, leading to unintended command execution on the host system.", "vulnerable_example": "public String executeCommand(String command) throws IOException, InterruptedException {\n    if (command == null || command.isEmpty()) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Command cannot be null or empty\");\n    }\n\n    Process proc = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(command);\n    StringBuilder outputBuilder = new StringBuilder();\n\n    try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(proc.getInputStream()))) {\n        String line;\n        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {\n            outputBuilder.append(line).append(\"\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    int exitCode = proc.waitFor();\n    if (exitCode != 0) {\n        throw new IOException(\"Command execution failed with exit code: \" + exitCode);\n    }\n\n    return outputBuilder.toString().trim();\n}", "fixing_pattern": "To prevent command injection, the input should be sanitized to remove or escape special characters that could be used to inject additional commands. Alternatively, use a safer API that avoids shell interpretation, such as `ProcessBuilder` with explicit arguments.", "fixing_example": "public String executeCommand(String command) throws IOException, InterruptedException {\n    if (command == null || command.isEmpty()) {\n        throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Command cannot be null or empty\");\n    }\n\n    // Sanitize the command input\n    String sanitizedCommand = command.replaceAll(\"[^a-zA-Z0-9\\\\s\\\\-_.]+\", \"\");\n\n    String[] cmdArray;\n    if (System.getProperty(\"os.name\").toLowerCase().contains(\"win\")) {\n        cmdArray = new String[]{\"cmd.exe\", \"/c\", sanitizedCommand};\n    } else {\n        cmdArray = new String[]{\"sh\", \"-c\", sanitizedCommand};\n    }\n\n    Process proc = new ProcessBuilder(cmdArray).start();\n    StringBuilder outputBuilder = new StringBuilder();\n\n    try (BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(proc.getInputStream()))) {\n        String line;\n        while ((line = reader.readLine()) != null) {\n            outputBuilder.append(line).append(\"\\n\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    int exitCode = proc.waitFor();\n    if (exitCode != 0) {\n        try (BufferedReader errorReader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(proc.getErrorStream()))) {\n            String errorLine;\n            while ((errorLine = errorReader.readLine()) != null) {\n                outputBuilder.append(errorLine).append(\"\\n\");\n            }\n        }\n        throw new IOException(\"Command execution failed with exit code: \" + exitCode);\n    }\n\n    return outputBuilder.toString().trim();\n}"}
