{"pattern_name": "Race Condition Due to Double Fetch", "functionality": "The function fetches user-provided data from user space and uses it to perform operations without ensuring the data remains consistent between fetches.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code fetches user-provided data (karg) from user space and then uses it to verify the adapter (ioc) without ensuring the data remains consistent between the fetch and the verification.", "vulnerable_example": "if (copy_from_user(&karg, uarg, sizeof(struct mpt_ioctl_eventreport))) {\n  printk(KERN_ERR MYNAM \"%s@%d::mptctl_eventreport - \"\n    \"Unable to read in mpt_ioctl_eventreport struct @ %p\\n\",\n    __FILE__, __LINE__, uarg);\n  return -EFAULT;\n}\nif (((iocnum = mpt_verify_adapter(karg.hdr.iocnum, &ioc)) < 0) ||\n  (ioc == NULL)) {\n  printk(KERN_DEBUG MYNAM \"%s::mptctl_eventreport() @%d - ioc%d not found!\\n\",\n    __FILE__, __LINE__, iocnum);\n  return -ENODEV;\n}", "fixing_pattern": "The fix removes the double fetch by passing the adapter (ioc) directly to the function, ensuring that the data used for verification is consistent and not subject to race conditions.", "fixing_example": "static int\nmptctl_eventreport (MPT_ADAPTER *ioc, unsigned long arg)\n{\n  struct mpt_ioctl_eventreport __user *uarg = (void __user *) arg;\n  struct mpt_ioctl_eventreport  karg;\n  int    numBytes, maxEvents, max;\n  if (copy_from_user(&karg, uarg, sizeof(struct mpt_ioctl_eventreport))) {\n    printk(KERN_ERR MYNAM \"%s@%d::mptctl_eventreport - \"\n      \"Unable to read in mpt_ioctl_eventreport struct @ %p\\n\",\n      __FILE__, __LINE__, uarg);\n    return -EFAULT;\n  }\n  dctlprintk(ioc, printk(MYIOC_s_DEBUG_FMT \"mptctl_eventreport called.\\n\",\n    ioc->name));\n  numBytes = karg.hdr.maxDataSize - sizeof(mpt_ioctl_header);\n  maxEvents = numBytes/sizeof(MPT_IOCTL_EVENTS);\n  max = MPTCTL_EVENT_LOG_SIZE < maxEvents ? MPTCTL_EVENT_LOG_SIZE : maxEvents;\n  if ((max < 1) || !ioc->events)\n    return -ENODATA;\n  ioc->aen