{"pattern_name": "Unauthenticated Encryption Mode", "functionality": "The code initializes an encryption context using AES-256-CBC mode, deriving a key and initialization vector (IV) from a provided password. It sets up the encryption context for subsequent use in encrypting data.", "vulnerable_pattern": "The code uses AES-256-CBC, an unauthenticated encryption mode, which does not provide integrity or authenticity guarantees. This can lead to vulnerabilities such as tampering or data manipulation, as the encrypted data can be altered without detection.", "vulnerable_example": "const EVP_CIPHER* cipher = EVP_aes_128_cbc(); // Using AES-128-CBC, another unauthenticated mode", "fixing_pattern": "To resolve this vulnerability, switch to an authenticated encryption mode such as AES-GCM, which provides both confidentiality and integrity. This ensures that the encrypted data cannot be tampered with without detection.", "fixing_example": "const EVP_CIPHER* cipher = EVP_aes_256_gcm(); // Using AES-256-GCM, an authenticated encryption mode"}
